  "source": "https://sudokupad.app/439w9opvs4",
  "title": "Double Take",
  "author": "Flinty & palpot",
  "rules": "Normal sudoku rules apply. Place the digits 1 to 9 in each Row, Column, and 3X3 box.\n\nEvery clue number outside the grid appears exactly twice. One appearance is a Full Rank clue and the other is an X-sums clue. It is up to the solver to determine the nature of each clue.\n\nThe digits on columns and rows, read in both directions, make a total of 36 numbers of nine digits each.\nFull Rank clues outside the grid have a value equal to the rank for the indicated row/column among those 36 numbers, where the lowest is 1 and the highest is 36.\n\nX-Sums clues outside the grid give the sum of the first X digits in their respective row or column, where X is the digit nearest the clue.",
  "solution": "259143867681759423743826519897512346135964782462387951576238194914675238328491675"
 },
